    <briefdescription>
<para><computeroutput><ref refid="classthrust_1_1constant__iterator" kindref="compound">constant_iterator</ref></computeroutput> is an iterator which represents a pointer into a range of constant values. This iterator is useful for creating a range filled with the same value without explicitly storing it in memory. Using <computeroutput><ref refid="classthrust_1_1constant__iterator" kindref="compound">constant_iterator</ref></computeroutput> saves both memory capacity and bandwidth. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>The following code snippet demonstrates how to create a <computeroutput><ref refid="classthrust_1_1constant__iterator" kindref="compound">constant_iterator</ref></computeroutput> whose <computeroutput>value_type</computeroutput> is <computeroutput>int</computeroutput> and whose value is <computeroutput>10</computeroutput>.</para>
<para><programlisting><codeline><highlight class="normal">#include<sp/>&lt;thrust/iterator/constant_iterator.h&gt;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">thrust::constant_iterator&lt;int&gt;<sp/>iter(10);</highlight></codeline>
<codeline></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">*iter;<sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>//<sp/>returns<sp/>10</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">iter[0];<sp/><sp/>//<sp/>returns<sp/>10</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">iter[1];<sp/><sp/>//<sp/>returns<sp/>10</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">iter[13];<sp/>//<sp/>returns<sp/>10</highlight></codeline>
<codeline></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">//<sp/>and<sp/>so<sp/>on...</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting></para>
<para>This next example demonstrates how to use a <computeroutput><ref refid="classthrust_1_1constant__iterator" kindref="compound">constant_iterator</ref></computeroutput> with the <computeroutput>thrust::transform</computeroutput> function to increment all elements of a sequence by the same value. We will create a temporary <computeroutput><ref refid="classthrust_1_1constant__iterator" kindref="compound">constant_iterator</ref></computeroutput> with the function <computeroutput>make_constant_iterator</computeroutput> function in order to avoid explicitly specifying its type:</para>
<para><programlisting><codeline><highlight class="normal">#include<sp/>&lt;thrust/iterator/constant_iterator.h&gt;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">#include<sp/>&lt;thrust/transform.h&gt;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">#include<sp/>&lt;thrust/functional.h&gt;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">#include<sp/>&lt;thrust/device_vector.h&gt;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">int<sp/>main()</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">{</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/>thrust::device_vector&lt;int&gt;<sp/>data{3,<sp/>7,<sp/>2,<sp/>5};</highlight></codeline>
<codeline></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/>//<sp/>add<sp/>10<sp/>to<sp/>all<sp/>values<sp/>in<sp/>data</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/>thrust::transform(data.begin(),<sp/>data.end(),</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>thrust::make_constant_iterator(10),</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>data.begin(),</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>::cuda::std::plus&lt;int&gt;());</highlight></codeline>
<codeline></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/>//<sp/>data<sp/>is<sp/>now<sp/>[13,<sp/>17,<sp/>12,<sp/>15]</highlight></codeline>
<codeline></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/>return<sp/>0;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">}</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting></para>
<para><simplesect kind="see"><para>make_constant_iterator </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
